# Compiled binaries.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH ON PURPOSE. An unanchored "scalpmcp" matches at
# every depth, so it also matched the cmd/scalpmcp DIRECTORY and silently kept
# the entire server out of the first commit — the module published, resolved,
# and then failed with "does not contain package". Keep these anchored.
/scalpmcp
/scalpmcp.exe
*.test

# Never commit a key. The server reads EVM_BASE_PRIVATE_KEY from the
# environment and writes it nowhere; these patterns exist so a local scratch
# file holding one cannot be committed by accident.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
